The 3D Video menu also chooses the depth layouts of a video with its depth map (picture and depth map side by side or one above the other, either first; with graphics; over a background) and turns the views drawn from depth maps on and off; Swap Left and Right Eyes is offered for 3D video only.

A 3D Video Settings window holds what is the program's: Enable 3D, the shortcut to KDE's display settings (where the screen's 3D mode is chosen), and for the video playing its input format (every packing and the depth layouts) and the swap of its left and right eyes. The input format and the swap are kept with the file they were chosen for, next to the other per-file choices of the program, and are unmarked again when they return to their default.

The 3D Video strings in Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, French, German, Japanese, Korean and Chinese, Simplified and Traditional (dragon-3d-video.po.patch of the edition's translations, 40 strings), the menu of patch 0001 among them.

debian/control: depends on Qt Multimedia +stereo3d14, which draws the views from depth maps, and on kde-cli-tools and kscreen, which the Display Settings shortcut starts (kcmshell6 kcm_kscreen).

The 3D Video menu and the 3D Video Settings window offer to save the 3D correction of a video into the file (ORDER 411). The offer appears only when a correction is set (an input format the person chose, or the swap of the eyes), the video is shown in 3D and it is a file on this computer; the question comes first, and nothing is written until the person says yes. The shared library libstereo-av (stereo_mark_save) writes the packing and the eye order: Matroska and WebM StereoMode (the depth layouts, StereoMode 15 to 20, included), MP4 and MOV st3d. The file is read back; on success the stored choice of the video is unmarked and the file is read again as it is. A refusal says why and what to do, leaves the file as it was and keeps the choice: a depth layout into MP4 (st3d has no depth value), a layout WebM cannot name, a stream that declares its own layout, an MP4 header with no room for the mark, mkvpropedit missing, a half or full size choice that the shape of the video does not give.

The strings of the offer in Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, French, German, Japanese, Korean and Chinese, Simplified and Traditional (28 more strings in dragon-3d-video.po.patch, 68 in all).

debian/control: also depends on mkvtoolnix, whose mkvpropedit writes Matroska files, and builds against libstereo-av-dev and libstereo-policy-dev 1.13.0 (stereo-layer 1.13.0, which carries the writers); the tests need ffmpeg and mkvtoolnix.

This entry also carries the depth work of 4:26.04.0-1+stereo3d6, which was staged and never published.
